{
  "category": "womens_bottoms",
  "version": "0.1",
  "notes": [
    "Every attribute includes 'unknown' so the extractor is never forced to guess.",
    "selection 'single' means exactly one value; 'multi' means a list of zero or more values.",
    "Use unknown when evidence is missing; use none only for explicitly supported absence. Never combine unknown, none, or not_applicable with other multi values.",
    "Use not_applicable only when the known garment type rules out an attribute, such as skirt_length for trousers. Unknown garment type is not evidence of non-applicability.",
    "pant_length applies to pants, shorts, leggings, and the shorts portion of a skort; skirt_length applies to skirts and the skirt portion of a skort.",
    "bottom_type identifies the garment; leg_shape describes its cut. Wide-leg trousers remain trousers with leg_shape wide.",
    "Prefer a specific bottom_type when explicit, such as cargo_pants or joggers. Use other for supported types outside the vocabulary.",
    "For fabric_type prefer blend for explicitly mixed fibers; do not infer stretch, opacity, or weight from fiber alone.",
    "Closure is multi so button and zip combinations can be captured. Generic button or zip wording does not establish closure_position.",
    "Do not infer pockets, belt loops, lining, solid pattern, or single-color construction from silence.",
    "Only extract facts about the product, not suggested outfits or coordinating items. Subjective occasion and style_tags should be soft ranking boosts.",
    "Source category Bottoms alone does not verify gender. Apply within the intended womenswear catalog scope.",
    "Start with priority attributes, then add others as descriptions support them. Preserve exact measurements, fiber percentages, and source metadata separately."
  ],
